Your project uses **MSTest 3.8.0**, which includes Microsoft Testing Platform (MTP) — so hot reload is supported. Here's the setup:

### 1. Add the hot reload package

```bash
dotnet add package Microsoft.Testing.Extensions.HotReload
```

### 2. Create `Properties/launchSettings.json`

```json
{
  "profiles": {
    "TestProject": {
      "commandName": "Project",
      "environmentVariables": {
        "TESTINGPLATFORM_HOTRELOAD_ENABLED": "1"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### 3. Run with hot reload (filtered to your failing test)

```bash
export TESTINGPLATFORM_HOTRELOAD_ENABLED=1
dotnet run --project . -- --filter "FullyQualifiedName~RemoveStock_ExceedsAvailable_ThrowsException"
```

The test host will run the test and **stay alive**. Edit your code, and it automatically re-runs — no rebuild needed. Press `Ctrl+C` when done.

